<h3>Notes:</h3>

<p>127.0.0.1 should be in your jail's address list, and your jail's primary IP should not be shared with any other jail.</p> <p>A FreeBSD jail without 127.0.0.1 in its address list has its loopback traffic rewritten to use the jail's primary address. Steam rejects this traffic because it appears to come from a non-loopback address. If you are getting persistent "Unexpected transport error" messages, this is likely the cause. FreeBSD only allows jails to share a single address from one family, so if your jail's primary IP is already being shared, you cannot share the loopback address.</p>
